Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
# --- GTK4 + libadwaita runtime ----------------------------------------
# The wizard is written in Python with PyGObject bindings against
# libadwaita (so it follows the GNOME visual language). The Trixie
# stack:
#   python3-gi               PyGObject 3.50
#   gir1.2-gtk-4.0           GTK 4 typelib
#   gir1.2-adw-1             libadwaita 1.5 typelib
#   libadwaita-1-0           libadwaita runtime
 python3-gi,
 gir1.2-gtk-4.0,
 gir1.2-adw-1,
 libadwaita-1-0,
# --- PolicyKit for the elevated `apt install` calls ------------------
# The wizard runs as the user, then drives apt via pkexec with a custom
# policy (shipped in files/). On Trixie the legacy policykit-1 transition
# package has been retired — depend on the actual daemon + pkexec
# directly.
 polkitd,
 pkexec,
# --- apt itself (for the install call) -------------------------------
 apt,
# --- Runtime deps of the post-install scripts ------------------------
# The install scripts under /usr/share/aims-os/install/ fetch upstream
# .deb files and APT repo GPG keys; they need curl, gnupg (for
# --dearmor) and ca-certificates. unzip is pulled lazily by
# runtimes.sh if missing; we Depend on it here too so the
# offline / standalone-apt path doesn't trip.
 curl,
 gnupg,
 ca-certificates,
 unzip,
Description: AIMS OS — first-boot wizard + post-install scripts
 Ships the first-boot wizard that lets a fresh AIMS OS user pick
 their track (Regular Maths, Coop Big Data, Coop Computer Security)
 plus any optional desktop extras (Chromium, GIMP, Inkscape, …) or
 the heavy dev stack (Java, Android, Docker, …).
 .
 The wizard auto-starts at the first GNOME session via an XDG
 autostart entry, checks connectivity, then runs `apt install` via
 pkexec with a bundled policy. After the first successful run it
 marks itself done in ~/.config/aims-welcome.done and stays silent
 unless the user re-launches it from the app grid.
 .
 Also ships the standalone post-install scripts at
 /usr/share/aims-os/install/ that handle the tools without a Debian
 package or a third-party apt repo we can rely on:
 .
   nodejs.sh    NodeSource Node 22 LTS apt repo + install nodejs
   vscodium.sh  Paulcarroty apt repo + install codium
   cursor.sh    Cursor .deb fetched from cursor.com (proprietary)
   dbeaver.sh   dbeaver.io apt repo + install dbeaver-ce
   runtimes.sh  Bun + Deno + uv from upstream GitHub releases
   rstudio.sh   RStudio Desktop .deb fetched from Posit's S3 bucket
 .
 The wizard calls these via pkexec; advanced users can run them by
 hand: `sudo /usr/share/aims-os/install/cursor.sh`.
 .
 The Python source for the wizard ships in step 4 of the v2.1 plan;
 this release contains only the install-scripts layer.
